<article class="env-lemma" id="04LP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04LP">Lemma <span data-tag="04LP">40.10.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Assume $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ with $k$ a field. For any points $r, r' \in R$ there exists a field extension $k'/k$ and points $r_1, r_2 \in R \times _{s, \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')$ and a diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ R &  R \times _{s, \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k') \ar[l]_-{\text{pr}_0} \ar[r]^\varphi &  R \times _{s, \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k') \ar[r]^-{\text{pr}_0} &  R }  \]
</div>
  <p> such that $\varphi $ is an isomorphism of schemes over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')$, we have $\varphi (r_1) = r_2$, $\text{pr}_0(r_1) = r$, and $\text{pr}_0(r_2) = r'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/02YF" data-tag="02YF">40.7.1</a> parts (1) and (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>